# Civil Rights vs. Civil Liberties: The Case of Discriminatory Verbal Harassment.

**Authors:** Grey, Thomas C.

## Abstract
One of the principal drafters of Stanford University's regulation concerning verbal harassment on campus proposes an interpretation of the conflict between civil rights and civil liberties in this situation. Contrasts in the two approaches to injury and the public/private distinction are highlighted. The text of Stanford's regulation is appended. (MSE)

